    "created_at": "2024-08-26T00:02:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-26T00:02:21Z",
    "body": "> Is there a reason to skip the view-transition, vs just running it with whatever elements are enabled?\r\n\r\nIt's the inverse, if the element was render-blocking only because it was required by a view transition and the UA has hit an internal timeout then the Document no longer needs to stay blocked on that element. In Blink that timeout is 4s.",
